# 03 - PC Setup

## PC-A (admin / staff host + console client)

| Item | Setting |
|------|---------|
| Role | Console client and VLAN 10 host |
| Console | USB-to-RJ45 cable to switch console port |
| Terminal | PuTTY or Tera Term, Serial, 9600 8N1, flow control None |
| LAN cable | Fa0/1 |
| NIC addressing | Obtain IP address automatically (DHCP) |
| Expected lease | 192.168.10.21/24, gateway 192.168.10.1 |

## PC-B (guest host)

| Item | Setting |
|------|---------|
| Role | VLAN 20 host |
| LAN cable | Fa0/25 |
| NIC addressing | Obtain IP address automatically (DHCP) |
| Expected lease | 192.168.20.21/24, gateway 192.168.20.1 |

## Useful Windows commands

```
ipconfig /release
ipconfig /renew
ipconfig /all
ping 192.168.10.1
ping 192.168.20.1
tracert 192.168.10.1
arp -a
```

Run PuTTY SSH from PC-A with:

```
ssh netadmin@192.168.99.1
```

If Windows has the OpenSSH client enabled, the command above also works from Command Prompt.

> Tip: disable other network adapters (Wi-Fi) on both PCs while testing so traffic and DHCP leases only use the lab NIC.
